            {
                "entry_id": "1a5aaef1-f45e-39c2-a598-47772583d2f4",
                "word": "buller",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "96afb2df-7837-415e-b87e-59a913bca844",
                        "entry_id": "1a5aaef1-f45e-39c2-a598-47772583d2f4",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "bullers"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3e615144-f119-38a5-8a44-1f56fe5c62b2",
                        "entry_id": "1a5aaef1-f45e-39c2-a598-47772583d2f4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A steer that allows itself to be mounted by bulls when in the crowded conditions of a feedlot."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fbf1cf3c-2f08-44d0-9bf8-849d42061004",
                                "sense_id": "3e615144-f119-38a5-8a44-1f56fe5c62b2",
                                "text": "Male cattle ('riders') in intensive housing are prone to mount herdmates willing to stand to be mounted ('bullers'). The buller-steer syndrome has been estimated to cost $70 per head, which can represent significant losses in large feedlots (Blackshaw et al., 1997). Incidence of bullers in a feedlot was about 2% (409 bullers in 20,428 mixed breed steers, Irwin et al., 1979)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2122e28b-8a50-4e08-a332-f66ba3ddb82e",
                                "sense_id": "3e615144-f119-38a5-8a44-1f56fe5c62b2",
                                "text": "The annual incidence of buller steers within the feedlot industry is reported to fall between 2 and 4 percent, but the incidence per pen can be quite variable ranging from 0.0 percent to 11.2 percent per pen (Taylor et al., 1997)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "94c4be6f-90ca-4b07-ba1a-430c7db73b4b",
                                "sense_id": "3e615144-f119-38a5-8a44-1f56fe5c62b2",
                                "text": "Buller steers are often injured from persistent mounting by pen mates, or debilitated to the point that they must be removed from the group and housed separately. The added labor and pens required to manage buller steers cuts into profit margins. Losses are even greater when buller steers become debilitated."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "172f0f27-d9ce-3ed8-985f-a6b03c1183f4",
                        "entry_id": "1a5aaef1-f45e-39c2-a598-47772583d2f4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A homosexual man."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Caribbean",
                            "Jamaica",
                            "derogatory"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ee5f9e4-cadc-4ae3-9c6b-d078918e7942",
                                "sense_id": "172f0f27-d9ce-3ed8-985f-a6b03c1183f4",
                                "text": "My mother always mentioned these teachings when she saw a buller man or heard about someone thought to be a buller."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fc778bcc-46f7-4506-ba01-dd6be5307b76",
                                "sense_id": "172f0f27-d9ce-3ed8-985f-a6b03c1183f4",
                                "text": "This process of articulating my own story and asking other bullers to make public their stories is an attempt to assert and broaden the reality of Black male same-sex existence, which too many people for far too long have tried to erase."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "41202b4c-2cf7-44e9-b7d7-2b3c5c55f4d7",
                                "sense_id": "172f0f27-d9ce-3ed8-985f-a6b03c1183f4",
                                "text": "“Well, day say yuh must be ah buller man,” the pastor said flatly."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
