                        "form": "bullered"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "90caf6d0-1a32-3fb0-8c28-07413047847b",
                        "entry_id": "df4201a9-b99f-334e-b423-7551ffbe29a2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To make a lot of noise."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "47080f81-6f93-49fd-9f78-53d5ad69d505",
                                "sense_id": "90caf6d0-1a32-3fb0-8c28-07413047847b",
                                "text": "\"Sae we let go the rape,” said David, “ and he went adown the water screeching and bullering like a Bull of Bashan, as he's ca'd in Scripture.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e07b65d5-c065-4ae7-9f4d-4b2e6b01a8cc",
                                "sense_id": "90caf6d0-1a32-3fb0-8c28-07413047847b",
                                "text": "It never shrinked nor feared, but would dowk under the water, snorting and bullering, terrible to the hearers and beholders."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6eb57d73-fbce-4a12-8635-1e82f4b9ed06",
                                "sense_id": "90caf6d0-1a32-3fb0-8c28-07413047847b",
                                "text": "On the other side there lay a lighted suburb, which we thridded for a while, then turned into a dark lane, and presently found ourselves wading in the night among deep sand where we could hear a bullering of the sea."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f5e8ec5e-74c9-3190-a529-a59e1575bb81",
                        "entry_id": "df4201a9-b99f-334e-b423-7551ffbe29a2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To force one's way; to be pushy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a64f0c54-f183-4bd7-a1a3-3d4dd8868816",
                                "sense_id": "f5e8ec5e-74c9-3190-a529-a59e1575bb81",
                                "text": "It was not that he bullered and swore like so many of his farmer neighbours. Their men knew what to expect from them, and they swore back, knowing that the next day they could speak to them as if nothing had happened. But Will Murray was different. His word was law."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "90f5ea0a-767d-4e46-9c58-a1b6d9653962",
                                "sense_id": "f5e8ec5e-74c9-3190-a529-a59e1575bb81",
                                "text": "The door of the vet's banged open and the receptionist bullered out."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "32e8fa7a-f5c0-417e-a12d-29f4532c21cb",
                                "sense_id": "f5e8ec5e-74c9-3190-a529-a59e1575bb81",
                                "text": "But it's Christmas the morn's morn — It bullered, throbbed like a U-boat, black."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
